      "type": "'auto' | 'full'",
      "default": "'full'",
      "defaultValue": "full",
      "options": [
        "auto",
        "full"
      ],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "divider",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "How far the bottom rule under the strip runs.\n\n- `full` — one rule across the whole container, drawn by md-tabs itself\n  and running past the last tab to the container's edge. **The default.**\n- `auto` — each tab draws its own 1px segment, so the rule is exactly as\n  wide as the tabs collectively are.\n\n`full` IS THE DEFAULT because `auto` only looks right in the one case\nwhere the strip happens to fill its container — `tab-width=\"equal\"`. In a\nwide panel at `tab-width=\"auto\"`, a few content-sized tabs leave the rule\nstopping partway across and the panel below appears to hang off the end of\nit, which reads as a bug rather than a choice. `auto` remains available for\na strip that genuinely should be bounded by its tabs.\n\nIn `full` mode the per-tab segments are suppressed by setting\n`--md-tab-divider-color: transparent` on the host — custom properties\ninherit through the slotted tabs' shadow roots, so there is no second\nsource of truth about which mode is active."
    },
    {
      "name": "ariaLabelProp",
      "type": "string",
      "default": "''",
      "defaultValue": "",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": false,
      "attribute": "aria-label",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Accessible label for the tablist"
    },
    {
      "name": "tabWidth",
      "type": "string",
      "default": "'equal'",
      "defaultValue": "equal",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": false,
      "attribute": "tab-width",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "How tabs size along the strip. All modes are layout-stable under\ndynamic content (labels/badges can change without reshuffling the\nstrip); long labels ellipsize instead of forcing a tab wider.\n- `equal` (default) — tabs share the parent's FULL width equally;\n  tracks change only when the PARENT resizes.\n- `auto` — each tab takes its content width (the strip scrolls), so\n  tracks follow content by design.\n- any CSS length (e.g. `\"140px\"`, `\"10rem\"`) — every tab gets exactly\n  that width regardless of parent or content."
    },
    {
      "name": "width",
      "type": "string",
      "default": "''",
      "defaultValue": "",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": false,
      "attribute": "width",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Explicit width for the WHOLE strip (any CSS size: `\"480px\"`, `\"40rem\"`,\n`\"100%\"`). By default the strip is `100%` of its parent — in\nshrink-to-fit layouts (inline-block cards, auto grid columns, flex\nitems) that parent's width follows the ACTIVE TAB PANEL, so switching\nto a tab with tiny content collapses the whole tablist. Set `width` to\nanchor the strip regardless of what the panels do."
    }
  ],
